From ea886e871516f9e7842fb50fd989b6784632d384 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:27:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] BananaDS perf: Gengis frames overlap, VBlank waits for
 the conversion only (render.3d_pipeline)

At VBlank the emulator's thread waited for every bin of the 3D frame (Finish3DRendering -> WaitAll) and drew
the missing ones itself (render.gengis_help); under qemu on dsstress L5 that was 227 of 1188 bins, a third of
the thread's instructions. The frame's polygons and render registers are only read by the conversion (the first
thread to claim a bin copies them into gx_polys and a gx_frame), the bins read those copies, the texture flats
and the texture cache. So two frame slots now (gx_frame, polygons, rows, and their own copies of the pipeline's
DISP3DCNT / alpha reference / toon table blocks, gx_frame_init), bins claimed from one 64-bit word (gen << 32 |
next bin, so a claim is of a known frame), a done mask per slot:
- Finish3DRendering waits only for the frame's conversion (melonDS swaps its polygon RAM right after), and
  helps with it only with render.gengis_help=2 as before;
- a frame starts (line 215) once the slot it takes, the frame before last's, is drawn, and once every bin of the
  last frame is claimed (it helps or waits for those); texture or texture-palette VRAM changes still wait for
  every bin first (the bins read the flats and the cache);
- the 2D thread waits for each line's bin of the frame its job names (render.3d_wait2d; a slot holding a later
  frame means the job's frame was all drawn before it); the emulator's thread, when it does need a bin
  (X scroll, capture, no 2D thread), waits for the shown frame's, helping only with that frame's bins;
- savestates wait for every bin (PreSavestate), as do Reset and the end.
Off: VBlank waits for all the frame's bins as before. Same pictures: every read is ordered as it was, and
fused.c's per-thread texture alpha cache (f_begin_frame per frame gen) only chooses between kernels of the same
result. With no render threads nothing changes.

